cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8c89a268ff45e36e80dd73d1212d0f77aeff480e" commit="b690b154078911e8c738aa45ce4ff43029762acf" commit_message="camera: intel: ipu3: Remove the log for shutter done ahead of time  The log just checks the request sequence in the ResultProcessor, it does nothing for the code logic, remove it.  BUG=b:119070747 TEST=Build and deploy package to platform and camera works  Change-Id: I8c89a268ff45e36e80dd73d1212d0f77aeff480e Signed-off-by: Yang Liang &lt;liang.l.yang@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1461643 Commit-Ready: Wei Meng &lt;wei.meng@intel.corp-partner.google.com&gt; Tested-by: Wei Meng &lt;wei.meng@intel.corp-partner.google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-yu Wu &lt;hywu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei Meng &lt;wei.meng@intel.corp-partner.google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1461643" owner_email="wei.meng@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/43/1461643/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iba95e9eb43cac4c01b8f66fcf82fc3deb947fecb" commit="152893a638541b575e0afc91c53bb918bdc373fa" commit_message="tcpc/mt6370: Fix keeps entering/leaving LPM when sink device attached.  When usb-c port is attached, TCPM will make TCPC leave LPM by calling tcpm_init-&gt;mt6370_init.  However, mt6370_init will do soft reset in the function, and mt6370 is not able to report the correct CC status via auto-toggle when soft reset is done while usb-c port being plugged with a sink device (source device is fine in this case).  This CL only allows doing soft reset when it is woken up from the shipping mode.  This can solve the issue since that it won't woken up by a source device.  BRANCH=None BUG=b:122017882 TEST=1. cutoff; plugged pd charger, and see EC running normal.      2. Plug a sink device, and see the TCPC move its states to non-LPM;         unplug hub, and see it in LPM.      3. Plug a nothing connected hub, and see mt6370 move its states         to non-LPM; unplug the hub, and see mt6370 in LPM.      3. Plug a nothing connected hub, and see mt6370 move its states         to non-LPM; plug a charger to the hub, and see mt6370 sinking         power from the hub.      4. Plug pd charger, and see the TCPC move its state to LPM.  Change-Id: Iba95e9eb43cac4c01b8f66fcf82fc3deb947fecb Signed-off-by: Yilun Lin &lt;yllin@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1442391 Commit-Ready: Yilun Lin &lt;yllin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yilun Lin &lt;yllin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jett Rink &lt;jettrink@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1442391" owner_email="yllin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/91/1442391/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8ad88482e1805397561c967e4f2d556af455538d" commit="035ce059b28fdc2cb45b7a22e3146d1919edd1ec" commit_message="mtpd: Add newly needed syscalls to seccomp filter.  https://crrev.com/83cad55244685bd6ed53018b0b9e2762030f919e caused libusb to be compiled with udev support. With udev support, libusb does udev device enumeration on initialization, which uses these syscalls.  Although mtpd uses udev, its usage is simpler and didn't use these syscalls previously.  BUG=chromium:929968 TEST=Build and deploy onto nocture (x86-64) and peach_pit (armv7) +      Plug in MTP device and browse files.  Change-Id: I8ad88482e1805397561c967e4f2d556af455538d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1466201 Commit-Ready: Anand Mistry &lt;amistry@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Anand Mistry &lt;amistry@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1466201" owner_email="a